{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>All the soul coming to Jacob.</b> That they went out from the land of Canaan to come to Egypt; and this 'coming' is not past tense but present tense, as in ״בָּעֶרֶב הִיא בָאָה״ (Esther 2:4), and as in ״וְהִנֵּה רָחֵל בִּתּוֹ בָאָה עִם הַצֹּאן״ (Genesis 29) — therefore its accent is below, on the alef, because when they set out to come from the land of Canaan they were only sixty-six. And the second, ״כָּל הַנֶּפֶשׁ לְבֵית יַעֲקֹב הַבָּאָה מִצְרַיְמָה שִׁבְעִים״ — that is past tense; therefore its accent is above, on the bet, because once they arrived there they were seventy, for they found Joseph and his two sons there, and Yocheved was added to them between the walls. And according to the one who says twins were born with the tribes, we must say that they died before their descent to Egypt, for they are not counted here. I found in Vayikra Rabbah: Esav had six souls, and Scripture calls them 'souls of his house,' in the plural, because they served many divinities; Jacob had seventy, and Scripture calls them 'one soul,' because they served one El."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 46, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:03:44.695708509Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}